Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by an off-by-one error in the condition that checks whether the descriptor array needs to be expanded. The original condition incorrectly allowed for the possibility of exceeding the allocated size of the `descs` array, leading to memory overflow and corruption of the container structure during send operations. This overflow resulted in crashes when the send completion process accessed invalid memory locations.

Here is the patch:
 /* tx not dword sized - pad */
 int _pad_sdma_tx_descs(struct hfi1_devdata *dd, struct sdma_txreq *tx)
 {
 	int rval = 0;

-	if ((unlikely(tx->num_desc + 1 == tx->desc_limit))) {
+	if ((unlikely(tx->num_desc == tx->desc_limit))) {
 		rval = _extend_sdma_tx_descs(dd, tx);
 		if (rval) {
 			__sdma_txclean(dd, tx);
 			return rval;
 		}
 	}

 	/* finish the one just added */
 	make_tx_sdma_desc(
 		tx,
 		SDMA_MAP_NONE,
 		dd->sdma_pad_phys,
 		sizeof(u32) - (tx->packet_len & (sizeof(u32) - 1)),
 		NULL, NULL, NULL);
 	tx->num_desc++;
 	_sdma_close_tx(dd, tx);
 	return rval;
 }



